  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday morning through next Friday)\nIssued at 242 PM EDT Sat Sep 12 2026\n\nBy Monday morning the main frontal boundary from the short term will \nhave moved south of the state with high pressure continuing to build \nback into the area. This ridge will also bring in a drier airmass \ninto central GA with a slightly drier airmass keeping things dry \nthrough at least Days 5 to 6 (Wed and Thu).  Current model runs show \na wave moving back into the region from the Atlantic Thu evening \ninto Fri which could increase precipitation chances. for now just \ngoing with a 20% chance for Fri afternoon and will see over the \nnext few days how the models handle this.  \n\nTemps will stay in the upper 80s to middle 90s through day 7 but \nwith the drier airmass moving in Heat index values will slowly fall \nthrough Thursday . Min Dewpoints Mon and Tue will be in the upper \n60s to lower 70s but they will fall into the lower to middle 60s by \nWed. Even with temps still in the lower 90s it will feel a lot more \ncomfortable.",
